  "title": "Answer: no position on space, and consciousness depends on the front of the brain",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "fe6c0689-be6e-4b8b-91d7-178dc4c4ea7f",
      "text": "The view takes no position on what space is. Huxley's one spatial claim concerns the brain: consciousness depends on the anterior division of the brain, while the spinal cord and lower centers can carry out complex actions with no consciousness at all.",
